# Register File

## Goal

Build a small multi-register Register File in Verilog and understand how CPUs use registers to store temporary data and provide operands to the ALU.

The Register File will support two simultaneous read operations and one write operation.

---

# What is a Register File?

A Register File is a collection of registers that can be accessed using register addresses.

A CPU uses registers to store values that are currently being used by instructions.

              Register Address
                     │
                     ▼
              ┌─────────────┐
              │             │
              │ Register    │
              │    File     │
              │             │
              └─────────────┘
                     │
                     ▼
                   Data

---

# Specifications

| Parameter | Value                  |
|-----------|------------------------|
| Number of Registers | 8            |
| Register Width      | 8 bits       |
| Read Ports          | 2            |
| Write Ports         | 1            |
| Write               | Synchronous  |
| Read                | Asynchronous |

The number of bits required for a register address is:

log2(8) = 3 bits

Therefore, a 3-bit address can select any of the 8 registers.

